  "reasoning": "The patient describes a 'silver-like dusting' on the skin along with peeling skin on the arms and back. This presentation is highly characteristic of psoriasis, a chronic immune-mediated skin condition classically defined by well-demarcated erythematous plaques covered with silvery-white scales (often described clinically as a silver dusting). While other conditions like fungal infections, drug reactions, or allergies can cause rashes or peeling, they typically lack this specific silvery scaling appearance. The combination of silvery scaling and skin peeling strongly points to psoriasis as the correct diagnosis.",
